  "id": "COMPOUND:24024 - PROTEIN:5798",
  "verbalization": "Callyspongenol B appears to interact with NH-6 through a series of molecular targets, with the most direct link being its interaction with Carboxylesterase 2, which is targeted by 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One. This compound, in turn, has a target relationship with NH-6. Similarly, Callyspongenol B is also shown to interact with SNB-78 and SF-188, which are both targeted by the same 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One. These findings suggest that Callyspongenol B may act through a common pathway involving this compound, which then targets NH-6. The evidence supports a mechanism where Callyspongenol B influences the activity of a shared intermediate, 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One, which ultimately leads to the interaction with NH-6. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Callyspongenol B in modulating the activity of this intermediate, which may have broader implications for its biological effects.",
